    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d643">

                <pb facs="0776" n="632" sameAs="frus:frus1929v02/pg632"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.933/183</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chinese Minister</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">C.
                        C. Wu</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Assistant Secretary of State</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-12-03">December 3, 1929</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Johnson</hi>: Herewith the memorandum you
                    wanted yesterday which I have been able to prepare with the present available
                    material.</p>
                <p>Will you let me know when you will be ready for the next Conference?</p>
                <p>I thank you for your promptness in sending me copy of the American Government’s
                    communication last evening.<anchor n="29" xml:id="d643-f1"/></p>
                <p>Yours very sincerely,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Chao-Chu Wu</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d643-a1.xml" xpointer="d643-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d643-f1" n="29" xml:id="d643-f1-content">
                <p>Presumably relating to the conflict between China and the Soviet Union; see the
                    Secretary’s statement of December 2, 1929, Department of State, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Press Releases</hi>, December 7, 1929 (Publication No.
                    23), p. 83.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
